window.docContents[49].resolve({"/part-2-analysis/ch06-convergence/#ch06-convergence":{"contents":"Every real sequence s : \\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{R} extends canonically to a hypersequence {}^*s : \\mathbb{N}^* \\to \\mathbb{R}^*. In Ch06_Convergence.lean (2,580 lines), the three pillars of classical sequence theory become one-line halo statements at unlimited indices N \\in \\mathbb{N}^* \\setminus \\mathbb{N}:\n\n* Convergence: \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} s_n = L iff {}^*s_N \\approx_h L for every unlimited N \\in \\mathbb{N}^*_\\infty.* Monotone Convergence: If s is monotone increasing and bounded above by M \\in \\mathbb{R}, then for any fixed unlimited \\omega, {}^*s_\\omega is limited, so L = \\mathrm{sh}({}^*s_\\omega) is the limit!* Bolzano–Weierstrass & Cauchy Completeness: If s is bounded, then for any unlimited \\omega, {}^*s_\\omega is limited and its shadow L = \\mathrm{sh}({}^*s_\\omega) is a cluster point; if s is Cauchy, {}^*s_M \\approx_h {}^*s_N for all unlimited M, N, forcing every unlimited index into the same halo \\mathrm{hal}(L).\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt\nopen Goldblatt.Ch06\n\n-- Hypersequences preserve monotonicity, bounds, and algebraic operations:\n#check @starSeq_mono\n#check @starSeq_le_coe_of_forall_le\n#check @isUnlimitedNat_add_right\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part II — Elementary Analysis via Infinitesimals","header":"2.1. Chapter 6: Sequences, Series & Robinson's Tail Criterion","id":"/part-2-analysis/ch06-convergence/#ch06-convergence"}});